<section class="faq-section">
  <div>
    
    <!-- FAQ -->
    <div class="faq-list">
      <button class="faq-question" type="button" data-modal="faq-project">
        Learn about the project
      </button>
      <button class="faq-question" type="button" data-modal="faq-exchanges">
        What about exchanges
      </button>
      <button class="faq-question" type="button" data-modal="faq-transactions">
        What about transactions
      </button>
      <button class="faq-question" type="button" data-modal="faq-bookkeeping">
        Bookkeeping page
      </button>
      <button class="faq-question" type="button" data-modal="faq-privacy">
        Is it private
      </button>
      <button class="faq-question" type="button" data-modal="faq-support">
        What does the project currently support?
      </button>
      <button class="faq-question" type="button" data-modal="faq-now">
        What are you working on now?
      </button>
      <button class="faq-question" type="button" data-modal="faq-tax">
        Is this tax software?
      </button>
      <button class="faq-question" type="button" data-modal="faq-wallet-vs-bookkeeping">
        Why is "Still in Wallet" different from my Vault balance?
      </button>
    </div>

    <div class="modal-overlay welcome-modal" id="faq-project">
      <div class="modal-content">
        <button class="modal-close" onclick="closeWelcomeModal(event)">×</button>

        <h1>Learn about the project</h1>

        <p>
          I have noticed a need in the industry. There's not really an
          open-source place for people to see what is inside their wallets. I
          feel that we should be able to open our wallet and know exactly what
          is inside. This information is displayed in the vault page of the
          wallet. You will find a watchlist, a place to add wallets and I'm not
          sure what will end up on the end. The second row will be a place where
          your wallets will sit. Each wallet will show their content -The chain
          and total value of the wallet will be displayed, underneath, you will
          see the number of days since a coin was transferred into your
          ecosystem. Maybe, you bought it, traded for it, or it was sent to you.
          Either way, you will know if it's short or long term capital gaines.
          You will see the ticker symbol, amount dollar value and profit/loss.
          The same wallet, with a divider will show Aave DeFi projects, with the
          loan health at the top of the list. Then, will display the dollar
          value of the loan, dollar value of your collateral, and break down
          your collateral. The last section will show NFTs. I didn't realize
          that there were so many in my wallet. Most of them were useless, so
          there's a hide button. If you're like me and obsess over having hidden
          something of value, you can always unhide it.
          <strong>you can delete any tin that you wish</strong>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="modal-overlay welcome-modal" id="faq-exchanges">
      <div class="modal-content">
        <button class="modal-close" onclick="closeWelcomeModal(event)">×</button>

        <h1>What about exchanges</h1>

        <p>
          You can add exchanges. The self-custody wallets pull data from APIs,
          exchanges use CSV files. You can just upload the file into the
          project. There's no industry standard format for the csv files, so one
          file may have a table with five columns beginning with gas fees, while
          the other may have ten columns beginning with a unique user ID that
          nobody understands except people who work with databases. So, each
          exchange has a unique upload. These tins will display the tokens in
          your account. and push your transactions to the bookkeeping page for
          storage.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="modal-overlay welcome-modal" id="faq-transactions">
      <div class="modal-content">
        <button class="modal-close" onclick="closeWelcomeModal(event)">×</button>

        <h1>What about transactions</h1>

        <p>
          It is easiest to start from the selling point and work our way back to
          the beginning. When you sell, trade or send a coin, the coin is gone.
          We can only do this once, so planning this end just makes sense. You
          need to know before you sell if you will make a profit and how old the
          coin is. Its funeral could cost you a lot of profit if you don't plan
          its execution carefully. That's why I built the bookkeeping page.
          Coins are grouped. For example if you received this coin in your
          self-custody wallet from your exchange wallet that information is
          noted, the sending transaction and receiving action are coupled
          together, so that it's obvious. However that coin made its way into
          your exchange wallet is also part of the group, so you have a clear
          picture of its age, and profit / loss. If the coin mysteriously
          appeared in your wallet, every attempt will be made to find the value
          of that coin when it first appeared.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="modal-overlay welcome-modal" id="faq-bookkeeping">
      <div class="modal-content">
        <button class="modal-close" onclick="closeWelcomeModal(event)">×</button>

        <h1>Bookkeeping page</h1>

        <p>
          This is where my project should help lots of people. They can see all
          their transactions in one place. They can see their realized gaines
          on this page. They can download either list. they can add notes to
          each transaction. Maybe, one day I will think of other things to put
          on this page, but for now I think this information is so powerful,
          it's all the page needs.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="modal-overlay welcome-modal" id="faq-privacy">
      <div class="modal-content">
        <button class="modal-close" onclick="closeWelcomeModal(event)">×</button>

        <h1>Is it private</h1>

        <p>
          Short answer, no. Everything pulled from the API keys is out there for
          the public to see. But, the website is private, your login is private
          and your data is secure. The database encrypts everything. I will
          eventually track unique Ids, number of wallets, what features people
          are using, and how much traffic. My purpose is to measure my
          effectiveness, and make a better product.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="modal-overlay welcome-modal" id="faq-support">
      <div class="modal-content">
        <button class="modal-close" onclick="closeWelcomeModal(event)">×</button>

        <h1>What does the project currently support?</h1>

        <ul>
          <li>
            self-custody wallets:
            <ol>
              <li>
                wallet value, age of coins, coins, amount of coins, their value
                and profit/loss
              </li>
              <li>Aave Defi health, loan amount, collateral amount, then listed coins</li>
              <li>
                NFTs -with the option to hide and unhide all, webpages that have
                interacted with the wallet
              </li>
            </ol>
          </li>
          <li>
            Exchange wallets: You can upload a CSV file into your tin, and the
            transactions will be passed to the bookkeeping page. Because there's
            no standardized format for CSV files from exchanges, each one is
            uploaded differently. Only some are supported.
          </li>
          <li>
            Coin Tracking: Each coin has a lifecycle as it makes its way through
            your finances. From the incubators of inception, to the cold hard
            tomb of defeat, each transaction is grouped to the same coin. The
            final resting place is the snapshot view.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="modal-overlay welcome-modal" id="faq-now">
      <div class="modal-content">
        <button class="modal-close" onclick="closeWelcomeModal(event)">×</button>

        <h1>What are you working on now?</h1>

        <ol>
          <li>
            The tin inside bookkeeping called "allTransactions" does not scroll. I'm
            sure there's a great reason for this, but I am not sure what it is.
            They all should download, and I am working to get them to scroll.
          </li>
          <li>
            I am exploring options with the API calls. The free APIs plan has its
            quirks and doesn't always want to do what I want. I want things to
            load much faster than they do.
          </li>
          <li>
            The allTransactions tin in the vault doesn't scroll either. It's there
            temporarily. I am not sure what I will put in its place yet. Any ideas??
          </li>
          <li>
            I want to revamp the add a wallet. I am not sure why it says I have
            $0.04, and I'll try not to spend it all at once, but I would like one
            place that users import their wallet and exchange tins. I'm thinking
            that I will put a drop-down menu instead of stretching different
            exchanges across the bottom of the screen. The problem is that it just
            looks bare without wallets. This is short term. Longer term I want to
            add functionality to other chains.
          </li>
          <li><strong>1/30 I saw my first subscriber today.  I was thankful for the person, but felt bad because there was no documentation.</strong>As we enjoyed a snow day at home, I wrote documentation for my project, and for the first time I feel like someone noticed its worth.  -so thankful.</li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="modal-overlay welcome-modal" id="faq-wallet-vs-bookkeeping">
      <div class="modal-content">
        <button class="modal-close" onclick="closeWelcomeModal(event)">×</button>

        <h1>Why is "Still in Wallet" different from my Vault balance?</h1>

        <p>
          These two numbers measure the same assets in completely different ways — and both are correct. Here's the difference:
        </p>

        <p>
          <strong>Vault — Market Value</strong><br />
          The Vault pulls live data directly from the blockchain right now. The dollar value shown is what your coins are worth <em>today</em> at current market prices. If you bought Bitcoin in 2018 for $6,000 and it's now worth $90,000, the Vault shows $90,000.
        </p>

        <p>
          <strong>Bookkeeping — Cost Basis</strong><br />
          "Still in Wallet" on the Bookkeeping page shows what you <em>originally paid</em> for the coins you haven't sold yet — your cost basis. Using the same example, it would show $6,000 for that Bitcoin. This number matters for taxes: when you eventually sell, your taxable gain is the difference between what you sell it for and what you paid (the cost basis).
        </p>

        <p>
          <strong>In short:</strong> Vault = current market value of your portfolio. Bookkeeping = what you paid to build it. The gap between the two is your unrealized profit (or loss).
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="modal-overlay welcome-modal" id="faq-tax">
      <div class="modal-content">
        <button class="modal-close" onclick="closeWelcomeModal(event)">×</button>

        <h1>Is this tax software?</h1>

        <p>
          This project is still in beta mode, but should provide valuable information
          for your taxes and every year you use it, and the more data you give it,
          the more effective it will be.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <style>
    /* Page centering container */
    .welcome-page {
      min-height: 70vh;
      display: flex;
      justify-content: center;
      align-items: center;
      padding: 2rem;
    }

    /* Card */
    .hero-card {
      width: 100%;
      max-width: 360px;
      background: #121212;
      border-radius: 16px;
      overflow: hidden;
      box-shadow: 0 12px 30px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.35);
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
    }

    /* Image */
    .hero-image img {
      width: 100%;
      height: auto;
      display: block;
    }

    /* Info section */
    .hero-info {
      padding: 1.25rem;
      text-align: center;
    }

    .hero-info h2 {
      margin: 0;
      font-size: 1.3rem;
      font-weight: 600;
    }

    .hero-role {
      font-size: 0.9rem;
      opacity: 0.75;
      margin: 0.25rem 0 1rem;
    }

    /* Social buttons */
    .hero-links {
      display: flex;
      gap: 0.5rem;
    }

    .hero-links a {
      flex: 1;
      text-decoration: none;
      font-size: 0.8rem;
      padding: 0.55rem;
      border-radius: 8px;
      background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.06);
      color: white;
      transition: all 0.2s ease;
      text-align: center;
    }

    .hero-links a:hover {
      background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.15);
      transform: translateY(-2px);
    }

    .faq-list {
      display: grid;
      gap: 0.6rem;
      margin-top: 1.5rem;
    }

    .faq-question {
      width: 100%;
      text-align: left;
      padding: 0.85rem 1rem;
      border-radius: 12px;
      border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.12);
      background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.05);
      color: #fff;
      font-size: 0.98rem;
      cursor: pointer;
      transition: border-color 0.2s ease, background 0.2s ease, transform 0.2s ease;
    }

    .faq-question:hover {
      background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);
      border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.28);
      transform: translateY(-1px);
    }

    /* modal */
    .modal-overlay {
      position: fixed;
      top: 0;
      left: 0;
      width: 100%;
      height: 100%;
      background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.7);
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: center;
      z-index: 9999;
    }

    .welcome-modal {
      display: none;
    }

    .welcome-modal.is-open {
      display: flex;
    }

    .modal-content {
      background: #121212;
      color: #ffffff;
      max-width: 600px;
      width: 90%;
      padding: 2rem;
      border-radius: 14px;
      box-shadow: 0 0 40px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.6);
      position: relative;
      animation: modalFadeIn 0.3s ease;
    }

    .modal-close {
      position: absolute;
      top: 12px;
      right: 14px;
      background: none;
      border: none;
      font-size: 1.5rem;
      color: #aaa;
      cursor: pointer;
    }

    .modal-close:hover {
      color: #fff;
    }

    @keyframes modalFadeIn {
      from {
        opacity: 0;
        transform: scale(0.95);
      }
      to {
        opacity: 1;
        transform: scale(1);
      }
    }
  </style>

  <script>
    const modals = Array.from(document.querySelectorAll(".welcome-modal"));

    /** @param {Event} event */
    function closeWelcomeModal(event:any) {
      const targetModal =
        event?.currentTarget instanceof HTMLElement
          ? event.currentTarget.closest(".welcome-modal")
          : null;

      if (targetModal) {
        targetModal.classList.remove("is-open");
      }
    }

    document.querySelectorAll("[data-modal]").forEach((trigger) => {
      trigger.addEventListener("click", () => {
        const id = trigger.getAttribute("data-modal");
        if (!id) return;
        const modal = document.getElementById(id);
        if (modal) {
          modal.classList.add("is-open");
        }
      });
    });
  </script>
</section>
